    title: "Nessus: install & scan a target VM",
    description:
      `Install Nessus Essentials, run a Basic Network Scan against a local vulnerable VM (Metasploitable2), and analyse/categorise the findings by severity. This is the automated-vulnerability-scanning counterpart to the manual Nmap lab — you'll see how much a scanner finds in minutes versus what it takes to find and verify by hand, and why triage-by-severity matters before you touch anything.`,
